{
  "id": "BP-PLATFORM-01-register-tenant",
  "bp_entry": "BP-PLATFORM-01",
  "title": "Register a tenant as a configurable process: start, run, step log, mail, retry, designer edit, rollback, refusals",
  "description": "The pilot scenario of the tenant registration (T-2744 step A, T-2608 steps B..H). Step A reads the shipped definition (read-only). B..G run in the platform tenant as the platform administrator and create throwaway tenants uat-tmp-<uuid> only: B starts a registration from the route (202) and checks that the engine ARMED the first step (B2) and that the platform step RAN (B3; the two steps name the two causes of an instance that sits in started: nothing armed, or the step runner off on the host); C the instance COMPLETES, the step log lists the six steps in order, the tenant is active with its realm bound; D the mail is in Mailpit; E a forced failure (a realm the bind step refuses) ends in ERROR, the timeline names the step, the DLQ entry is retried (second attempt shown); F a new draft through the designer API adds the file step, a path-like file name is refused at activation, the draft is activated, a start runs the file step, the first instance stays on version 1; G one call rolls back, a start has no file step; H a company user is refused on the start, the activation and the reads. The scenario adds the catcher domain to the platform tenant's outbound allow-list as the explicit step B0 (the notify step is refused at dispatch without it) and the cleanup removes it, deactivates every throwaway tenant (QA cannot purge a tenant made through the routes) and rolls the definition back if a step failed before G1; the platform residue block watches the definition and the instances. A4 is the one browser check: the Playwright spec web/tests/e2e/pilot-register-tenant-qa.e2e.spec.ts against the real designer page https://qa.bizdala.com/definitions/<id>, with the id of A1 supplied as QA_DESIGNER_URL and a signed-in platform administrator's saved browser state as QA_STORAGE_STATE. Inputs: realm (a realm id that exists on QA for the throwaway tenants), realm_bad (default uat-no-such-realm), hostname_suffix, stuck_after_s (default 60), run_within_s (default 120). Actors: admin = the platform administrator (an actor object of the platform tenant), storekeeper = a user of a company tenant. A3 reads the sorted catalogues by position (platform functions sorted by name; notification templates sorted by key, tenant_registered last): a new entry that sorts earlier moves a position and the step must be updated with it. NOT covered, named in the findings of T-2608: signing in as the new tenant's administrator (the runner has static actors and no provisioner flow yet) and a download route of the notification file (the file step is proved by its completed row in the step log).",
  "tenant": "${tenant}",
  "inputs": [
    "realm"
  ],
  "dry_run": {
    "tenant": "bpm-default",
    "actors": {
      "admin": {
        "user": "admin-user",
        "tenant": "bpm-default",
        "base_url": "https://qa.bizdala.com"
      },
      "storekeeper": "qoimeks-qa2-storekeeper"
    },
    "inputs": {
      "realm": "uat-tmp-fixture"
    }
  },
  "outputs": {},
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "actor": "admin",
      "says": "The platform administrator reads the active definition platform.register_tenant of the platform tenant: it exists, it is ACTIVE, version 1 or later.",
      "do": {
        "api": "GET",
        "path": "/api/v1/definitions/active/platform.register_tenant"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "json": {
          "$.name": "platform.register_tenant",
          "$.status": "ACTIVE",
          "$.version": {
            "regex": "^[1-9][0-9]*$"
          }
        }
      },
      "save": {
        "definition_id": "$.id",
        "version1": "$.version"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "actor": "admin",
      "says": "The graph the designer page loads: eight nodes, every service step carries its function name, the notify node carries a template and a recipient variable.",
      "do": {
        "api": "GET",
        "path": "/api/v1/definitions/${definition_id}"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "json": {
          "$.graph.nodes[7].node_type": "END",
          "$.graph.nodes[8]": {
            "absent": true
          },
          "$.graph.nodes[0].node_type": "START",
          "$.graph.nodes[1].id": "validate",
          "$.graph.nodes[1].attributes.platform_call.function": "tenant.validate",
          "$.graph.nodes[2].id": "create",
          "$.graph.nodes[2].attributes.platform_call.function": "tenant.create",
          "$.graph.nodes[3].id": "provision",
          "$.graph.nodes[3].attributes.platform_call.function": "tenant.provision",
          "$.graph.nodes[4].id": "bind_realm",
          "$.graph.nodes[4].attributes.platform_call.function": "tenant.bind_realm",
          "$.graph.nodes[5].id": "grant_first_admins",
          "$.graph.nodes[5].attributes.platform_call.function": "tenant.grant_first_admins",
          "$.graph.nodes[6].id": "notify",
          "$.graph.nodes[6].attributes.notify.template_key": "tenant_registered",
          "$.graph.nodes[6].attributes.notify.recipient.var": "admin_email"
        }
      },
      "requires": [
        "definition_id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "A3a",
      "actor": "admin",
      "says": "The function registry the designer's step panel reads (GET /api/v1/platform-functions): the entry of each function of the graph, by name.",
      "do": {
        "api": "GET",
        "path": "/api/v1/platform-functions"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "json": {
          "$.items[1].name": "tenant.bind_realm",
          "$.items[2].name": "tenant.create",
          "$.items[3].name": "tenant.grant_first_admins",
          "$.items[5].name": "tenant.provision",
          "$.items[6].name": "tenant.validate",
          "$.items[1].inputs[0].name": {
            "exists": true
          },
          "$.items[2].outputs[0].name": {
            "exists": true
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "A3b",
      "actor": "admin",
      "says": "The template options the notify step's picker reads (GET /api/v1/notification-templates/catalogue): the registered key tenant_registered and the placeholders it accepts.",
      "do": {
        "api": "GET",
        "path": "/api/v1/notification-templates/catalogue"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "json": {
          "$.items[7].template_key": "tenant_registered",
          "$.items[7].placeholders": {
            "contains": "tenant_name"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "B0a",
      "actor": "admin",
      "says": "B0. The platform tenant's allow-list: the mail channel is open (the seed of G14 opens channels only).",
      "do": {
        "api": "POST",
        "path": "/api/v1/outbound-destinations",
        "body": {
          "channel": "email"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 201
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "B0b",
      "actor": "admin",
      "says": "B0. The catcher domain of the QA mail trap is allowed for the platform tenant's notify step (the step is refused at dispatch without it). The cleanup removes it again.",
      "do": {
        "api": "POST",
        "path": "/api/v1/outbound-destinations",
        "body": {
          "channel": "email",
          "destination": "uat.letflow.internal"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 201
      },
      "save": {
        "domain_added": "$.destination"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "B0c",
      "actor": "admin",
      "says": "B0. The file channel is open for the platform tenant (a file step needs no destination).",
      "do": {
        "api": "POST",
        "path": "/api/v1/outbound-destinations",
        "body": {
          "channel": "file"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 201
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "B1",
      "actor": "admin",
      "says": "B. The platform administrator registers a throwaway tenant (uat-tmp-*) from the registration route: 202 with an instance id, no direct create or provision call.",
      "do": {
        "api": "POST",
        "path": "/api/v1/onboarding",
        "body": {
          "slug": "uat-tmp-${uuid1}",
          "display_name": "UAT registration ${run_id}",
          "hostname": "uat-tmp-${uuid1}.${hostname_suffix}",
          "idp_realm_id": "${realm}",
          "admin_email": "reg-${uuid1}@uat.letflow.internal"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 202,
        "json": {
          "$.instance_id": {
            "exists": true
          },
          "$.status": "ACTIVE"
        }
      },
      "save": {
        "instance_id1": "$.instance_id",
        "slug1": "$.slug"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "B2",
      "actor": "admin",
      "says": "B. The engine ARMED the first step: the timeline lists the validate step within the stuck limit. A red step here means no step was armed (the engine did not arm the platform step).",
      "do": {
        "api": "GET",
        "path": "/api/v1/instances/${instance_id1}/timeline"
      },
      "poll": {
        "within_s": "${stuck_after_s}",
        "interval_s": 2
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "json": {
          "$.steps[1].node_id": "validate"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "B3",
      "actor": "admin",
      "says": "B. The first step RAN: it is completed within the stuck limit (default 60 s). A red step here with the step still running means the platform step runner is off on the host (LETFLOW_START_PLATFORM_STEP_RUNNER missing; T-2703/T-2707): the instance sits in started and never runs.",
      "do": {
        "api": "GET",
        "path": "/api/v1/instances/${instance_id1}/timeline"
      },
      "poll": {
        "within_s": "${stuck_after_s}",
        "interval_s": 2
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "json": {
          "$.steps[1].result": "completed"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "C1",
      "actor": "admin",
      "says": "C. The instance runs to its end: COMPLETED.",
      "do": {
        "api": "GET",
        "path": "/api/v1/instances/${instance_id1}"
      },
      "poll": {
        "within_s": "${run_within_s}",
        "interval_s": 2
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "json": {
          "$.status": "COMPLETED"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "C2",
      "actor": "admin",
      "says": "C. The step log lists the six steps in order, each completed (who/when/duration are on the row; no value is on it).",
      "do": {
        "api": "GET",
        "path": "/api/v1/instances/${instance_id1}/timeline"
      },
      "poll": {
        "within_s": "${run_within_s}",
        "interval_s": 2
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "json": {
          "$.steps[1].node_id": "validate",
          "$.steps[1].result": "completed",
          "$.steps[2].node_id": "create",
          "$.steps[2].result": "completed",
          "$.steps[3].node_id": "provision",
          "$.steps[3].result": "completed",
          "$.steps[4].node_id": "bind_realm",
          "$.steps[4].result": "completed",
          "$.steps[5].node_id": "grant_first_admins",
          "$.steps[5].result": "completed",
          "$.steps[6].node_id": "notify",
          "$.steps[6].result": "completed",
          "$.steps[1].started_at": {
            "exists": true
          },
          "$.steps[1].duration_ms": {
            "exists": true
          },
          "$.steps[7].node_id": "end"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "C3",
      "actor": "admin",
      "says": "C. The new tenant exists, is active and has its realm bound (the first administrators are granted by the grant step; the tenant is signed-in capable only through the provisioner flow, which no step of this file replaces).",
      "do": {
        "api": "GET",
        "path": "/api/v1/tenants/${slug1}"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "json": {
          "$.slug": "${slug1}",
          "$.status": "active",
          "$.idp_realm_id": "${realm}"
        }
      },
      "requires": [
        "slug1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D1",
      "actor": "admin",
      "says": "D. The mail of the notify step is in the Mailpit trap (recipient and subject only; the body is never read).",
      "do": {
        "wait_mail": {
          "recipient": "reg-${uuid1}@uat.letflow.internal",
          "subject": "Tenant ${slug1} is registered",
          "within_s": 60
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "E1",
      "actor": "admin",
      "says": "E. A forced failure: a registration with a realm the bind step refuses.",
      "do": {
        "api": "POST",
        "path": "/api/v1/onboarding",
        "body": {
          "slug": "uat-tmp-${uuid2}",
          "display_name": "UAT registration ${run_id}",
          "hostname": "uat-tmp-${uuid2}.${hostname_suffix}",
          "idp_realm_id": "${realm_bad}",
          "admin_email": "reg-${uuid2}@uat.letflow.internal"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 202,
        "json": {
          "$.instance_id": {
            "exists": true
          },
          "$.status": "ACTIVE"
        }
      },
      "save": {
        "instance_id2": "$.instance_id",
        "slug2": "$.slug"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "E2",
      "actor": "admin",
      "says": "E. The instance ends in ERROR.",
      "do": {
        "api": "GET",
        "path": "/api/v1/instances/${instance_id2}"
      },
      "poll": {
        "within_s": "${run_within_s}",
        "interval_s": 2
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "json": {
          "$.status": "ERROR"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "E3",
      "actor": "admin",
      "says": "E. The timeline names the failed step (bind_realm) and the steps before it as completed.",
      "do": {
        "api": "GET",
        "path": "/api/v1/instances/${instance_id2}/timeline"
      },
      "poll": {
        "within_s": "${run_within_s}",
        "interval_s": 2
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "json": {
          "$.steps[3].node_id": "provision",
          "$.steps[3].result": "completed",
          "$.steps[4].node_id": "bind_realm",
          "$.steps[4].result": "failed",
          "$.steps[4].last_failure_kind": {
            "exists": true
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "E4",
      "actor": "admin",
      "says": "E. The failure is in the dead-letter list of the platform tenant.",
      "do": {
        "api": "GET",
        "path": "/api/v1/dlq?instance_id=${instance_id2}"
      },
      "poll": {
        "within_s": 60,
        "interval_s": 2
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "json": {
          "$.items[0].id": {
            "exists": true
          }
        }
      },
      "save": {
        "dlq_id": "$.items[0].id"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "E5",
      "actor": "admin",
      "says": "E. The platform administrator retries the entry: the failed step is dispatched once more (the realm stays refused, so it fails again; the retry is bounded, not a loop).",
      "do": {
        "api": "POST",
        "path": "/api/v1/dlq/${dlq_id}/retry",
        "body": {}
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": [
          200,
          202
        ]
      },
      "requires": [
        "dlq_id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "E6",
      "actor": "admin",
      "says": "E. The step log shows the second attempt of the failed step.",
      "do": {
        "api": "GET",
        "path": "/api/v1/instances/${instance_id2}/timeline"
      },
      "poll": {
        "within_s": "${run_within_s}",
        "interval_s": 2
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "json": {
          "$.steps[4].node_id": "bind_realm",
          "$.steps[4].attempts": {
            "regex": "^[2-9]$"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "F1",
      "actor": "admin",
      "says": "F. The designer edit through the API: a new draft version of platform.register_tenant with the file notification step after the mail step.",
      "do": {
        "api": "POST",
        "path": "/api/v1/definitions",
        "body": {
          "name": "platform.register_tenant",
          "version": "uat-${run_id}",
          "description": "UAT ${run_id}: file step added",
          "graph": {
            "edges": [
              {
                "id": "e1",
                "source": "start",
                "target": "validate"
              },
              {
                "id": "e2",
                "source": "validate",
                "target": "create"
              },
              {
                "id": "e3",
                "source": "create",
                "target": "provision"
              },
              {
                "id": "e4",
                "source": "provision",
                "target": "bind_realm"
              },
              {
                "id": "e5",
                "source": "bind_realm",
                "target": "grant_first_admins"
              },
              {
                "id": "e6",
                "source": "grant_first_admins",
                "target": "notify"
              },
              {
                "id": "e7",
                "source": "notify",
                "target": "notify_file"
              },
              {
                "id": "e8",
                "source": "notify_file",
                "target": "end"
              }
            ],
            "nodes": [
              {
                "id": "start",
                "node_type": "START"
              },
              {
                "attributes": {
                  "platform_call": {
                    "args": {
                      "name": {
                        "var": "name"
                      },
                      "slug": {
                        "var": "slug"
                      }
                    },
                    "function": "tenant.validate",
                    "reads": {
                      "name": "string",
                      "slug": "string"
                    },
                    "writes": {}
                  }
                },
                "id": "validate",
                "node_type": "SERVICE_TASK"
              },
              {
                "attributes": {
                  "platform_call": {
                    "args": {
                      "name": {
                        "var": "name"
                      },
                      "slug": {
                        "var": "slug"
                      }
                    },
                    "function": "tenant.create",
                    "reads": {
                      "name": "string",
                      "slug": "string"
                    },
                    "writes": {
                      "tenant_id": "string"
                    }
                  }
                },
                "id": "create",
                "node_type": "SERVICE_TASK"
              },
              {
                "attributes": {
                  "platform_call": {
                    "args": {
                      "tenant_id": {
                        "var": "tenant_id"
                      }
                    },
                    "function": "tenant.provision",
                    "reads": {
                      "tenant_id": "string"
                    },
                    "writes": {
                      "schema_name": "string"
                    }
                  }
                },
                "id": "provision",
                "node_type": "SERVICE_TASK"
              },
              {
                "attributes": {
                  "platform_call": {
                    "args": {
                      "realm_id": {
                        "var": "realm_id"
                      },
                      "tenant_id": {
                        "var": "tenant_id"
                      }
                    },
                    "function": "tenant.bind_realm",
                    "reads": {
                      "realm_id": "string",
                      "tenant_id": "string"
                    },
                    "writes": {}
                  }
                },
                "id": "bind_realm",
                "node_type": "SERVICE_TASK"
              },
              {
                "attributes": {
                  "platform_call": {
                    "args": {
                      "admin_email": {
                        "var": "admin_email"
                      },
                      "tenant_id": {
                        "var": "tenant_id"
                      }
                    },
                    "function": "tenant.grant_first_admins",
                    "reads": {
                      "admin_email": "string",
                      "tenant_id": "string"
                    },
                    "writes": {}
                  }
                },
                "id": "grant_first_admins",
                "node_type": "SERVICE_TASK"
              },
              {
                "attributes": {
                  "notify": {
                    "recipient": {
                      "var": "admin_email"
                    },
                    "template_key": "tenant_registered",
                    "values": {
                      "registered_by": {
                        "var": "admin_email"
                      },
                      "tenant_name": {
                        "var": "name"
                      },
                      "tenant_slug": {
                        "var": "slug"
                      }
                    }
                  }
                },
                "id": "notify",
                "node_type": "SERVICE_TASK"
              },
              {
                "id": "notify_file",
                "node_type": "SERVICE_TASK",
                "attributes": {
                  "notify": {
                    "channel": "file",
                    "template_key": "tenant_registered",
                    "file_name": "registration-notice",
                    "values": {
                      "registered_by": {
                        "var": "admin_email"
                      },
                      "tenant_name": {
                        "var": "name"
                      },
                      "tenant_slug": {
                        "var": "slug"
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "end",
                "node_type": "END"
              }
            ]
          },
          "copy_variable_schemas_from": "${definition_id}"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 201,
        "json": {
          "$.status": "DRAFT"
        }
      },
      "save": {
        "definition_id2": "$.id"
      },
      "requires": [
        "definition_id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F2",
      "actor": "admin",
      "says": "F. The designer's live check accepts the graph.",
      "do": {
        "api": "POST",
        "path": "/api/v1/definitions/${definition_id2}/validate",
        "body": {}
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200
      },
      "requires": [
        "definition_id2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F3",
      "actor": "admin",
      "says": "F. A refusal: a draft whose file step names a path (../x) is created, and its activation is refused.",
      "do": {
        "api": "POST",
        "path": "/api/v1/definitions",
        "body": {
          "name": "platform.register_tenant",
          "version": "uat-bad-${run_id}",
          "description": "UAT ${run_id}: a path-like file name",
          "graph": {
            "edges": [
              {
                "id": "e1",
                "source": "start",
                "target": "validate"
              },
              {
                "id": "e2",
                "source": "validate",
                "target": "create"
              },
              {
                "id": "e3",
                "source": "create",
                "target": "provision"
              },
              {
                "id": "e4",
                "source": "provision",
                "target": "bind_realm"
              },
              {
                "id": "e5",
                "source": "bind_realm",
                "target": "grant_first_admins"
              },
              {
                "id": "e6",
                "source": "grant_first_admins",
                "target": "notify"
              },
              {
                "id": "e7",
                "source": "notify",
                "target": "notify_file"
              },
              {
                "id": "e8",
                "source": "notify_file",
                "target": "end"
              }
            ],
            "nodes": [
              {
                "id": "start",
                "node_type": "START"
              },
              {
                "attributes": {
                  "platform_call": {
                    "args": {
                      "name": {
                        "var": "name"
                      },
                      "slug": {
                        "var": "slug"
                      }
                    },
                    "function": "tenant.validate",
                    "reads": {
                      "name": "string",
                      "slug": "string"
